# Minerva's House Italian Salad

This was the Olive Garden-like standard salad served with the french baguettes (from Vermont Bakery) in the Sioux City, Iowa Minerva's.

It was a 50/50 blend of cut Romaine lettuce and Baby Field Greens, when the latter became widely available in the late 1990s.

## Ingredients

Lettuce mix, Romaine & Baby Field Greens
Red Onion, diced
Salami, matchstick
Black Olives, sliced
Green Olives, sliced
Roma Tomato, quartered lengthwise
Pepperoncini, whole (Greek)
Croutons

Olive Oil
Red Wine Vinegar
Italian Seasoning
Salt
Pepper

## Method

1. Using a stand mixer, whisk the Olive Oil, Red Wine Vinegar, spices, salt and pepper until it turns gray. Then mix for five more minutes. You can use a bit of prepared mustard to help with the emulsification, but they you'll need to balance with Lemon Juice and Sugar. Best to avoid it altogether. This dressing was notorious for separating.

2. Toss the Lettuce, Red Onion, Black Olives Green Olives and Salami with a measure of vinaigrette, until very lightly coated.

3. Add to serving dish. Garnish with Roma Tomato and Pepperoncini. Top with a few croutons.

4. Top with Parmesean Cheese, optional.

5. Serve with French Bread & Butter.
